.TH CYAML_GET 3 "2026-09-06" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cyaml_get \- navigate to a DOM node via a dot-separated path
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cyaml.h>

cyaml cyaml_get(cyaml root, const char *path);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Thin wrapper around _cyaml_get().  Navigate from root through a
dot-separated path and return the node at the destination.

Path syntax:
  - Components are separated by dots ('.').
  - A component beginning with '#' followed by one or more decimal
    digits indexes into a CYAML_LIST by position (e.g. "#0" is
    the first element).
  - All other components are treated as literal CYAML_DICTIONARY keys.
  - A bare '#' with no trailing digits has no valid index
    interpretation: when the current node is a CYAML_DICTIONARY it is
    used as a literal key (e.g. addressing a key literally named
    "#"), exactly like any other non-"#N" component; when the current
    node is a CYAML_LIST, there is no literal-key fallback for a list
    at all, so navigation fails and NULL is returned, matching cjson's
    own bare-'#' rejection for that case.
  - Escape sequences: '\e.' -> literal '.' in the key (not a
    separator); '\e\e' -> literal '\e' in the key.  A '\e' before any
    other character is left unchanged.
  - An empty component (nothing between two dots, or a leading or
    trailing dot) has no valid interpretation as either a literal
    empty-string key or a "#N" index, at any position in the path;
    navigation fails.

The returned reference is NON-OWNING.  It becomes invalid if the
containing node is mutated or destroyed.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
root  Root cyaml handle (typically CYAML_DICTIONARY or CYAML_LIST).
path  Dot-separated path string literal or char *.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Non-owning cyaml handle at the target, or NULL if root is NULL, any
component along the path is missing, the node type is incompatible,
or the path contains an empty component.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cyaml port = cyaml_get(doc, "server.ports.#0");
if (cyaml_type(port) == CYAML_INTEGER)
    printf("%lld\en", cyaml_int_val(port));

/* Top-level access with empty path returns root itself */
cyaml same = cyaml_get(doc, "");
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_set (3),
.BR _cyaml_get (3)
